PLAN = {
    # Week 1: Anchor Your Wake Time
    1: "**Week 1 - Day 1: Anchor Your Wake Time**\nPick your wake-up time right now (same time you'd want on a normal class day). Set the alarm. Tomorrow morning, get outside—even just onto a balcony or the front steps—for 10-15 minutes within 30 minutes of waking.",
    2: "**Week 1 - Day 2**\nSame wake time. Same morning-light walk. Notice what time you naturally get sleepy tonight—don't force anything yet, just notice.",
    3: "**Week 1 - Day 3**\nSame wake time, including if last night was a late one. This is the hard day—the pull toward 'sleeping in to catch up' is strongest here. Resist it; get the light instead.",
    4: "**Week 1 - Day 4**\nSame wake time and light. If mornings are cloudy or dark this time of year, a bright walk outside still works—it's the light intensity, not sunshine specifically, that matters.",
    5: "**Week 1 - Day 5**\nSame wake time and light. By now you may notice you're getting sleepy slightly earlier at night—that's your circadian clock responding.",
    6: "**Week 1 - Day 6 (Saturday-equivalent)**\nThis is the real test: hold the same wake time on a day with nothing scheduled. No sleeping in.",
    7: "**Week 1 - Day 7 (Sunday-equivalent)**\nSame wake time again. End of Week 1: your wake time should now feel less like an alarm fight and more like a habit.",

    # Week 2: Tame Your Caffeine Curve
    8: "**Week 2 - Day 8: Tame Your Caffeine Curve**\nCalculate your cutoff: target bedtime minus 8-10 hours (e.g., 11 p.m. bedtime = last caffeine by 1-3 p.m.). Write it somewhere visible. Continue fixed wake time + morning light.",
    9: "**Week 2 - Day 9**\nHit the cutoff. Swap your usual afternoon caffeine (if you'd normally have one) for water.",
    10: "**Week 2 - Day 10**\nCutoff again. If mornings feel rough without a second cup, that's normal in week one of any caffeine change—push through rather than pushing the cutoff later.",
    11: "**Week 2 - Day 11**\nCutoff again. Try swapping your morning/early afternoon coffee for matcha (caffeine + L-theanine) for a calmer energy boost, keeping L-theanine and caffeine strictly out of your 2-hour wind-down window (and obeying your 8-10 hour caffeine cutoff).",
    12: "**Week 2 - Day 12**\nCutoff again. Notice: are you actually reaching for caffeine out of tiredness, or out of habit/boredom? Either is fine to notice, just notice.",
    13: "**Week 2 - Day 13**\nCutoff again, even on a lighter day. Consistency here matters more than any single day's discipline.",
    14: "**Week 2 - Day 14**\nCutoff again. End of Week 2: your afternoons and evenings should now be caffeine-free, on top of your steady wake time.",

    # Week 3: Build Your Sleep Sanctuary
    15: "**Week 3 - Day 15: Build Your Sleep Sanctuary**\nSet up your room: crack a window, angle a fan, or adjust the thermostat toward the 60-67°F (15-19°C) range. Hang a towel over the worst light leak (streetlight, hallway light under the door) as a temporary blackout fix.",
    16: "**Week 3 - Day 16**\nMove your phone charger and laptop charger to a spot across the room, not within reach of the bed.",
    17: "**Week 3 - Day 17**\nIf you don't have blackout curtains yet, this is a good day to order a cheap eye mask as a stopgap.",
    18: "**Week 3 - Day 18**\nKeep the room cool and dark. Notice if you're waking up during the night—track roughly when, if you can.",
    19: "**Week 3 - Day 19**\nReinforce the bed-for-sleep rule: if you catch yourself studying or scrolling in bed today, relocate to a desk or chair, even mid-task.",
    20: "**Week 3 - Day 20**\nAdd background noise (a fan, white noise app) tonight if your space is loud—steady noise masks sudden disruptions without being stimulating.",
    21: "**Week 3 - Day 21**\nEnd of Week 3: room should now be cool, dark, and device-free within arm's reach on top of your wake time and caffeine habits.",

    # Week 4: Protect Your Wind-Down
    22: "**Week 4 - Day 22: Protect Your Wind-Down**\nWrite 2-3 if-then plans for this week (e.g., 'If it's [2 hours before bed], then I dim the lights and put my phone across the room'). Post them somewhere visible.",
    23: "**Week 4 - Day 23**\nExecute your if-then plan. Dim lights, step away from screens 2 hours before bed.",
    24: "**Week 4 - Day 24**\nSame wind-down, plus: finish dinner 2-3 hours before bed tonight.",
    25: "**Week 4 - Day 25**\nSame wind-down and meal timing. If you're hungry close to bed, favor something light (not heavy or high-sugar).",
    26: "**Week 4 - Day 26**\nSame routine. This is often the day the whole stack starts to feel automatic rather than effortful.",
    27: "**Week 4 - Day 27**\nSame routine, even under a busy or stressful day—this is exactly when the if-then plan earns its keep, since it removes the need to decide in the moment.",
    28: "**Week 4 - Day 28**\nSame routine. End of Week 4: wake time, caffeine cutoff, cool dark room, and a real wind-down should all be running together.",

    # Days 29-30: Consolidate
    29: "**Consolidate - Day 29**\nRun the full stack one more time, no new habits added. Notice what's felt automatic vs. what still takes effort.",
    30: "**Consolidate - Day 30**\nSame. Write down which single habit made the biggest felt difference—that's the one to protect first if life gets chaotic (finals, travel, a bad week). You don't need to keep adding; you just need this system to become boring and automatic."
